{"total_count":255,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/commits/c07d54aab0f17a425117ab073cb97aa4b78a5077","sha":"c07d54aab0f17a425117ab073cb97aa4b78a5077","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTU0NzM5NTk3OmMwN2Q1NGFhYjBmMTdhNDI1MTE3YWIwNzNjYjk3YWE0Yjc4YTUwNzc=","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/commit/c07d54aab0f17a425117ab073cb97aa4b78a5077","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/commits/c07d54aab0f17a425117ab073cb97aa4b78a5077/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/git/commits/c07d54aab0f17a425117ab073cb97aa4b78a5077","author":{"date":"2021-05-11T08:48:20.000+03:00","name":"George Necula","email":"gcnecula@gmail.com"},"committer":{"date":"2021-05-31T19:06:15.000+03:00","name":"George Necula","email":"gcnecula@gmail.com"},"message":"[jax2tf] Add shape polymorphism support for jnp.einsum.\n\nThe main problem was that jnp.einsum uses opt_einsum.contract_path\nto parse the specification string and compute the order or the\ncontractions. This function wants to compute the sizes of operands\nand intermediate results, and will fail if some dimensions are\npolymorphic.\n\nThe (partial) solution here is to replace the operands with\njax.ShapeDtypeStruct with a fixed size for all dimension variables,\nthen call opt_einsum.contract_path and use that result if there\nis only one contraction. We abort if there are multiple contractions.\nThis behavior is clearly sound. If there were multiple contractions,\nperhaps their order would be different with different dimension sizes.","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/git/trees/a5844c1f64c4a3f6be0fd508dff7e5c438c62ecb","sha":"a5844c1f64c4a3f6be0fd508dff7e5c438c62ecb"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"gnecula","id":3890983,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTA5ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3890983?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnecula","html_url":"https://github.com/gnecula","fol